				"⣿⠇⠀⠀⠀",
				616,
				168
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Output): Convert build pipeline configuration to TypeScript\n\nMigrate the entire Output build pipeline configuration from JavaScript to TypeScript. This includes the core ESBuild entry point, VS Code bundling logic, exclusion lists, and the extensive suite of transform plugins (Inject, Replace, Rewrite, Polyfill) used to adapt the upstream Editor source for the Land environment.\n\nAll `.js` files in `Configuration/` have been renamed to `.ts` (or kept as `.js` where acting as runtime output templates) and strictly typed. The `Source/` directory now contains the canonical TypeScript implementations, while `Configuration/` serves as the compiled output target for the build process itself. This ensures type safety across the build tooling and aligns with the project-wide mandate for PascalCase naming and strict typing.",
			"SHA": "e963076a56c2adf413023ad7f13d66317411c2db"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-09T17:51:43Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠇⠀⠀⠀",
				616,
				168
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Output): Prettify ESBuild configuration and plugins\n\nReformat the entire Output build pipeline configuration from minified single-line JavaScript into readable, multi-line ES6+ syntax. This affects the core ESBuild entry point, the VS Code bundling logic, exclusion lists, and the extensive suite of transform plugins (Inject, Replace, Rewrite, Polyfill) used to adapt the upstream Editor source for the Land environment.\n\nNo logic changes were made; this is strictly a formatting pass to improve maintainability and diff readability for future development.",
			"SHA": "08f51160a0665cfc85487377f106540288a79f3b"
		}
	],
